# NWC agent-loop cron schedule
#
# THE RAG-SYNC LINE IS NOW OWNED BY A VERB — DO NOT HAND-INSTALL IT (ops#230).
#   pl loop schedule status                    what owns the schedule here?
#   pl loop schedule install --execute         install/refresh (idempotent, backed up)
#   pl loop schedule remove  --execute         take it out again
#   pl loop schedule install --host <role>     declare it on another machine
# The verb writes a MARKER-DELIMITED managed block, so re-installing rewrites
# rather than duplicates and removing takes out exactly what it put in. A
# hand-edited crontab is one nobody can verify or move: on 2026-08-02 this
# machine's crontab was simply EMPTY and the estate had been blind for 16 nights.
#
# The remaining lines below are installed by hand for now:
#   crontab -l > /tmp/cron.bak
#   cat /home/rob/nwp/scripts/agent-loop/crontab.entry >> /tmp/cron.bak
#   crontab /tmp/cron.bak
#   crontab -l    # verify
#
# Uninstall:
#   crontab -l | grep -v '/home/rob/nwp/scripts/agent-loop/' | crontab -
#
# Pause without uninstall — WRAPPER-ENFORCED per-part switches (deep-audit C0):
#   pl loop disable fix-loop        # stop the autonomous issue->MR poll only
#   pl loop disable respawn-drain   # stop the power-user instant re-spawn only
#   pl loop disable rag-sync        # stop RAG->issues (stage 1) only
#   pl loop disable webhook         # make the webhook receiver inert
#   pl loop disable all             # WRITE kill-switch (every part that CHANGES things)
#   pl loop disable oversight       # OVERSIGHT kill-switch (the read-only parts)
#   pl loop enable <part|all|oversight>   # re-arm; pl loop parts shows state
#
# TWO KILLS, NOT ONE (ops#230). `all` stops the parts that can change the
# estate; it does NOT stop rag-sync, which only reads and files issues. A switch
# meaning "do not let agents write" must never also mean "stop looking" — that
# conflation blinded the estate for 16 nights while every cron exited 0.
#
# State is host-local at ~/.config/nwp-loop/parts.state (each host is separate).
# The legacy sentinels still work and still mean "off":
#   touch /home/rob/nwp/.loop-paused        (WRITE kill);      rm to resume
#   touch /home/rob/nwp/.oversight-paused   (OVERSIGHT kill);  rm to resume
#   touch /home/rob/nwp/.rag-sync-paused    (rag-sync only);   rm to resume
#
# Secrets handling
# ----------------
# Do NOT put GITLAB_TOKEN inline in crontab. Instead, source it from an
# env file that lives in the operator's $HOME (gitignored):
#
#   echo 'GITLAB_TOKEN=<your-glpat-token>' >> ~/.nwp-agent-loop.env
#   chmod 600 ~/.nwp-agent-loop.env
#
# The cron line below sources that file before invoking the script.
# AGENT_LOOP_*: see agent-loop.sh header for the full list.

# Sync new NWC feedback entities to GitLab issues — every 15 minutes.
*/15 * * * * cd /home/rob/nwp/sites/nwc/dev && /usr/bin/ddev drush nwc-feedback:sync-to-gitlab --limit=10 >> /home/rob/nwp/logs/feedback-sync.log 2>&1

# Drive the agent-loop (issue → PR) — every 30 minutes; 1 issue per run.
0,30 * * * * . $HOME/.nwp-agent-loop.env && AGENT_LOOP_MAX_PER_RUN=1 /home/rob/nwp/scripts/agent-loop/agent-loop.sh

# Stage 1 of the §6 self-healing loop (ops#6): turn the live RAG state into
# tracked nwp/ops issues — daily at 04:30 UTC, just after the audit-awareness
# refresh (~04:00). Dev-side only (files issues; no bumps/deploys). Reads its
# token from .secrets.yml, so no env file is needed.
#
# DO NOT PASTE THIS LINE INTO A CRONTAB. `pl loop schedule install --execute`
# owns it (see the top of this file); it writes the same entry inside a managed
# block that can be verified, refreshed and removed by code. Kept here only so
# this file still documents what the loop is made of.
#   30 4 * * * /home/rob/nwp/scripts/agent-loop/rag-sync.sh >> /home/rob/nwp/logs/rag-sync.log 2>&1

# Log rotation — two-tier:
#   1. Size-based: gzip any uncompressed log >50M, so a runaway hour
#      doesn't fill the disk.
#   2. Age-based: delete gzipped logs older than 90 days, so the
#      ~/nwp/logs/ directory doesn't accumulate forever. 90 days is
#      a deliberate trade-off: long enough for a quarterly review of
#      what went wrong, short enough that disk usage stays bounded.
#      Untouched .log files (the live ones) are never deleted; only
#      .log.gz files are pruned. Adjust the +90 if a different
#      retention policy is needed.
5 4 * * * /usr/bin/find /home/rob/nwp/logs -name '*.log' -size +50M -exec gzip {} \;
10 4 * * * /usr/bin/find /home/rob/nwp/logs -name '*.log.gz' -mtime +90 -delete
